# Start the GNSS daemon when the KEPLER receiver's CHPP node appears, which is
# also the only moment it can do anything: the node exists once gnss-kepler has
# bound to its SPI device, and the receiver has been codeloaded by the modem
# driver before that. Activating from udev rather than an enabled unit keeps the
# daemon off boards that have no receiver.
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="gnss", KERNEL=="gnss0", TAG+="systemd", \
	ENV{SYSTEMD_WANTS}+="kepler-gnssd.service"
